  <title>Language switching</title>
  <p>
    Language switching can automatically change voices for document content and/or
    user-interface elements when spoken content has language information. You can also use
    commands to switch manually to a configured voice set.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Global voice set normally applies. When language switching is enabled, Orca can use a
    matching language-specific voice set. If Limit switching to configured voices is enabled,
    Orca switches only to languages for which you have configured a voice set. Language
    switching settings are part of Global Voice Settings preferences, the shared speech-behavior
    settings rather than a voice set. With that limit off, Orca can use any language supported
    by the synthesizer, even without a matching voice set. Selecting a language-specific voice
    set manually suspends automatic language switching until you return to the Global voice set.
  </p>
